Backport of llvm/llvm-project 585f04f2bf1 ([Support] Add missing include
for MacOS defines, #208065).

CrashRecoveryContext.cpp uses setpriority(PRIO_DARWIN_THREAD, ...) under
__APPLE__ without including <sys/resource.h>; the declaration and the
PRIO_DARWIN_* macros only ever arrived transitively through other LLVM and
libc++ headers. The Xcode 26 toolchain's libc++ no longer includes
<sys/resource.h> transitively, so the file stops compiling on macOS:

    error: use of undeclared identifier 'PRIO_DARWIN_THREAD'

Applies identically to LLVM 20.1.8 and 21.1.8 (the include block is the
same in both); upstream fixed it on main in July 2026.

--- a/llvm/lib/Support/CrashRecoveryContext.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Support/CrashRecoveryContext.cpp
@@ -15,5 +15,8 @@
 #include <cassert>
 #include <mutex>
 #include <setjmp.h>
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+#include <sys/resource.h>
+#endif
 
 using namespace llvm;
